            "review_title": "Review at La Cave de Saigon",
            "review_text": "PetaMay\nSingapore, Singapore375 contributions\n0\nHas a lot of potential\nSep 2018 • Couples\nDropped by this place several times over the past few months, always turned away at the door by a young man. Finally after calling, were able to determine the place is open and we could come here for a drink. On arrival, again the young man wanted to turn us away, until we insisted that we had called then allowed in.\n\nWine selection is pretty good for French wines and menu looks good although only had the cheese, but that was pretty good. The atmosphere is nice and has a lot of potential.\n\nBut, wine by the glass there is only a selection of white, red and sparkly. If yuo buy a glass of wine you can not use the proper red wine glasses, as a wine person you know how important the glass is for the wine the breath. And even though we were the only people there, we were rudely told we can not use those glasses.\n\nWine was not cheap, but had the atmosphere been more pleasant it would be worth it.\n\nThe same lady that told us about the glasses also sits by the front door on leaving making it very obvious that she is checking if anything is taken (i had a wet wipe in my hand).\nRead more\nValue\nService\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten September 24, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
